From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:57:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: Refuse new capture buffers while the
 session runs

Without dynamic buffer mode, as on the MSM8996 encoder, the capture
buffers are given to the firmware with HFI_CMD_SESSION_SET_BUFFERS once,
when both queues have started streaming. A buffer added afterwards with
VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS is queued to the firmware without having been set,
and the firmware dies on its first fill:

  qcom-venus c00000.video-codec: SFR message from FW: QC_IMAGE_VERSION_STRING=VIDEO.VE.4.4-00060 Err_Fatal - Z:\b\venus_proc\venus\utils\src\vbuffer.c:1219:

GStreamer's v4l2h264enc adds a capture buffer like this as soon as
downstream holds one, so every encode stopped after three frames.
Setting the new buffer at that point does not help: the firmware
answers HFI_ERR_SESSION_INCORRECT_STATE_OPERATION.

Return -EBUSY for such a CREATE_BUFS instead. GStreamer then carries on
with the buffers it has. The check needs the dynamic buffer mode test,
so export it as venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode().

Tested on an APQ8096 tablet (Samsung Galaxy Tab S3): 90-frame
GStreamer encodes at 1920x1080 and 3840x2160 now run to the end.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c |  9 +++++----
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h |  1 +
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c    | 10 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 59eee3dd9e..1224485745 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@ session_process_buf(struct venus_inst *inst, struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf)
 	return hfi_session_process_buf(inst, &fdata);
 }
 
-static bool is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst)
+bool venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst)
 {
 	struct venus_core *core = inst->core;
 	struct hfi_plat_caps *caps;
@@ -553,6 +553,7 @@ static bool is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst)
 
 	return caps->cap_bufs_mode_dynamic;
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode);
 
 int venus_helper_unregister_bufs(struct venus_inst *inst)
 {
@@ -560,7 +561,7 @@ int venus_helper_unregister_bufs(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	struct hfi_buffer_desc bd;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
+	if (venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
 		return 0;
 
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(buf, n, &inst->registeredbufs, reg_list) {
@@ -581,7 +582,7 @@ static int session_register_bufs(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	struct venus_buffer *buf;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
+	if (venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
 		return 0;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(buf, &inst->registeredbufs, reg_list) {
@@ -1306,7 +1307,7 @@ int venus_helper_set_dyn_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	struct hfi_buffer_alloc_mode mode;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
+	if (!venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
 		return 0;
 
 	mode.type = HFI_BUFFER_OUTPUT;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h
index 358e4f39c9..e98f9dd7ea 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.h
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ int venus_helper_set_num_bufs(struct venus_inst *inst, unsigned int input_bufs,
 int venus_helper_set_raw_format(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 hfi_format,
 				u32 buftype);
 int venus_helper_set_color_format(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 fmt);
+bool venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst);
 int venus_helper_set_dyn_bufmode(struct venus_inst *inst);
 int venus_helper_set_bufsize(struct venus_inst *inst, u32 bufsize, u32 buftype);
 int venus_helper_set_multistream(struct venus_inst *inst, bool out_en,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 627bc7ce5f..a67745ea0e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1111,6 +1111,16 @@ static int venc_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *q,
 		    sizes[0] < inst->output_buf_size)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * Without dynamic buffer mode the firmware is given the
+		 * capture buffers when the session starts and refuses new
+		 * ones while it runs. A buffer it was not given crashes it.
+		 */
+		if (q->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE &&
+		    inst->streamon_out && inst->streamon_cap &&
+		    !venus_helper_is_dynamic_bufmode(inst))
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		return 0;
 	}
 
